@user193767: The proof is by induction on $n$. If $n=1$, then $a_1 = 1$ and $a_2 = 1$, so $a_1 + a_2 = 2 = 2^1$. Assume that $a_1 + \cdots + a_n = 2^{n-1}$ for some $n > 1$. Then $a_1 + \cdots + a_{n+1} = (a_1 + \cdots + a_n) + a_{n+1} = 2^{n-1} + a_{n+1} = 2^{n-1} + 2^{n-1} = 2^n$. – Michael E2 Nov 1 '15 at 14:12

